{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_skkvm4gnwwotc6lfo4pcnqaw7bdh2uv4pu46nfkxgvovlxsnf25a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass: `test_tableau`, `test_encrypt`, `test_decrypt`.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- **`src/tableau.rs`** — Implemented `beaufort_tableau` to construct a square matrix where `mat[y][x] = alpha[(j + y) % size]` with `j` starting at `size` and decrementing per column, matching `c_src/src/tableau.c`.\n- **`src/encrypt.rs`** — Implemented `beaufort_encrypt`: when no matrix is provided (empty slice, equivalent to C's `NULL`), it generates one from `BEAUFORT_ALPHA`. For each input char, it locates the column whose top-row entry equals the char, finds the row in that column whose entry equals the current key char, and emits the leftmost char of that row. Pass-through behavior matches the C version (don't advance the key index `j` if the char/key isn't found).\n- **`src/decrypt.rs`** — Implemented the inverse: find the row whose first column equals the input char, find the column in that row matching the key char, emit the top-row char at that column. Same pass-through semantics.\n\nPer instructions, `src/lib.rs` and `src/bin/` were left unmodified — the remaining warnings come from those files. `cargo build` and `cargo test` both succeed (3/3 tests passing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":28848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0ec0784-d4f6-4968-afa4-500d72034877","uuid":"e5a0768b-3061-482c-bbf3-05078862e5b1"}
